#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Builds the six additional files (English and French) from the analysis outputs.

    python3 build_supplements.py            # write every .tex, compile, check
    python3 build_supplements.py --no-pdf   # write the .tex only

Rule: every number printed in an additional file is read from a CSV (or from a
file generated by the pipeline), never typed here. The only literals are design
constants copied from the code, each with the file and line it comes from.
Statements that interpret the numbers are guarded by assertions: if a new run
changed the data so that a sentence became false, the build stops.

Output, next to this script:
    Additional_file_1.tex ... Additional_file_6.tex          (English)
    Fichier_additionnel_1.tex ... Fichier_additionnel_6.tex  (French)
    the matching PDFs, and supplement_numbering.csv (table and figure numbers,
    used to fill the references of the main text).
"""
